DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLocati
 on: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwide
 .\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, roun
 d-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\, 
 and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and pr
 oduction (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: Appro
 ximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (July
  to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyar
 tcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:effea-call-5-festival-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: EFFEA Call #5: European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artis
 ts
DESCRIPTION:The European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artists (EFFEA)\, an i
 nitiative of the European Festivals Association co-funded by the European 
 Union\, opens its fifth call: 50 residencies for 50 emerging artists (indi
 viduals\, groups or collectives) hosted by partnerships of around 150 fest
 ivals\, each led by one leading festival with a minimum of two partner fes
 tivals from different eligible countries.\n\nOrganisation: European Festiv
 als Association (EFA)\nLocation: Residencies hosted by festival partnershi
 ps of at least three festivals from three eligible countries (most of Euro
 pe plus Tunisia and Ukraine). Leading festivals and artists must be based 
 in an eligible country\; festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\,
  Turkey and the UK may join as partner festivals only\, and artists from t
 hose countries may also be proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the
  artists\; artists cannot apply directly.\nAward: 50 residency grants: 40 
 Discovery grants of EUR 8\,000 (for artists at an early career stage) and 
 10 Springboard grants of EUR 15\,000 (for artists established at home and 
 ready to break through internationally). A minimum of 80 percent of the gr
 ant must cover costs incurred by the artists (fees\, travel\, accommodatio
 n\, subsistence). An own contribution of EUR 1\,000 (Discovery) or EUR 2\,
 000 (Springboard) is deducted from the paid grant. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Residencies implemented between 1 January and 31 December 2027\, c
 o-produced by one leading festival and at least two partner festivals\n\nM
 ore: https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residencies hosted by festival partnerships of at least three fest
 ivals from three eligible countries (most of Europe plus Tunisia and Ukrai
 ne). Leading festivals and artists must be based in an eligible country\; 
 festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\, Turkey and the UK may jo
 in as partner festivals only\, and artists from those countries may also b
 e proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the artists\; artists cannot
  apply directly.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:norma-fonds-projectbijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting NORMA: NORMA Fonds Project Grant (round 4\, 202
 6)
DESCRIPTION:The NORMA Fonds redistributes copyright remuneration collected 
 by Stichting NORMA into cultural\, social and professional projects involv
 ing performing artists\, and is one of the few Dutch schemes with four int
 akes a year and a genuinely short cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting NORMA 
 (collecting society for performing artists)\nLocation: Netherlands-based a
 rts-sector activity. No city or region restriction stated.\nAward: Maximum
  EUR 10\,000 per project. Total project budget may not exceed EUR 150\,000
  and the applicant organisation's annual budget may not exceed EUR 500\,00
 0. At least 25 percent of the project budget must come from audience or bo
 x-office revenue. Performer fees must meet the 2026 wage norms of EUR 139 
 per rehearsal and EUR 340 per performance. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 Single project\, typically a production or concert series. Final report du
 e within six months of completion.\n\nMore: https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/
 norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restrict
 ion stated.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultuurloket-digitall-implementatiebijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultuurloket DigitALL: Implementation Contribution (Imple
 mentatiebijdrage\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:A one-off 2026 call letting Dutch cultural institutions reuse a
 nd adapt digital technology that other institutions have already built and
  published in the open DigitALL Toolkit\, for example translation software
  shared between theatres or a streaming platform adapted for a new venue. 
 Grants run up to EUR 30\,000 and cover technical modification\, integratio
 n\, production and deployment costs.\n\nOrganisation: Cultuurloket DigitAL
 L\nLocation: Netherlands and the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom. No city o
 r region restriction.\nAward: Up to EUR 30\,000. Covers technical modifica
 tion\, system integration\, production and deployment costs. Hardware purc
 hase alone is ineligible unless clearly essential to the public experience
 . No stated co-financing percentage. No application fee.\nDuration: Not sp
 ecified\; scoped to a single implementation.\n\nMore: https://cultuurloket
 digitall.nl/implementatiebijdrage/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://cultuurloketdigitall.nl/implementatiebijdrage/?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands and the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom. No city or reg
 ion restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:simons-foundation-open-interval-turbulence-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Open Interval: An Artist-Scientist Exploration of Turbule
 nce
DESCRIPTION:Open Interval is a Simons Foundation program that supports trio
 s consisting of an artist\, a scientist\, and a representative from a 501(
 c)(3) arts organization to collaborate around a shared scientific theme. T
 he current cycle centers on the theme of turbulence\, a phenomenon at the 
 edge of chaos and beauty.\n\nOrganisation: Simons Foundation\nLocation: Un
 ited States (trio must be regionally co-located)\nAward: USD 30\,000 per a
 warded trio\nDuration: April to December 2027 (several months of collabora
 tion)\n\nMore: https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-ope
 n-interval-an-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.simonsfoundation.org/2026/06/01/coming-soon-open-interval-a
 n-artist-scientist-exploration-of-turbulence/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States (trio must be regionally co-located)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:blackbird-foundation-believers-fund-iii-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270630
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270701
SUMMARY:Deadline: Blackbird Foundation: Believers Fund III 2026
DESCRIPTION:Believers funds the people\, projects and programs creating the
  conditions for young people's creativity to flourish at scale. Creativity
  is meant in the broadest sense: artists are creative\, but so are scienti
 sts\, debaters\, community builders and dancers\, and a project can be any
 thing from a summer camp to a robotics competition to a co-working holiday
  house for artists.\n\nOrganisation: Blackbird Foundation\nLocation: Austr
 alia and/or New Zealand\; individuals\, groups or organisations establishe
 d in AU/NZ\, with projects taking place in AU/NZ.\nAward: AUD 5\,000 and A
 UD 10\,000 grants. No application fee.\nDuration: Projects must be complet
 ed within 12 months\n\nMore: https://www.blackbird.foundation/projects?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.blackbird.foundation/projects?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia and/or New Zealand\; individuals\, groups or organisatio
 ns established in AU/NZ\, with projects taking place in AU/NZ.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emap-emare-media-art-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART:20261106T123000Z
DTEND:20261106T130000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 14:00 CET: EMAP / EMARE: European Media Art Platform Resid
 encies 2027
DESCRIPTION:Closes 06 Nov 2026 at 14:00 CET.\n\nThe European Media Art Plat
 form (EMAP/EMARE) is a network of leading European media-art organisations
  offering fully funded two-month production residencies for artists workin
 g with digital media\, including media art\, bio art and robotic art.\n\nO
 rganisation: European Media Art Platform (EMAP / EMARE)\nLocation: Two-mon
 th production residency at one of 15 host institutions across Austria\, Fr
 ance\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Slovenia\, Croatia\, 
 Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Poland\nAward: EUR 
 4\,000 grant for the applying artist (including subsistence)\; EUR 2\,000 
 for a collaborating artist (EUR 6\,000 total for a duo)\; EUR 4\,000 proje
 ct budget\; accommodation provided by the host\; travel covered per EU cei
 lings\; access to technical facilities and media labs. No application fee.
 \nDuration: Two months\n\nMore: https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://call.emare.eu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Two-month production residency at one of 15 host institutions acro
 ss Austria\, France\, Slovakia\, Portugal\, Belgium\, Netherlands\, Sloven
 ia\, Croatia\, Spain\, Italy\, Cyprus\, Greece\, Latvia\, Germany and Pola
 nd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:foresight-ai-science-safety-nodes-grants@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T162448Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Foresight Institute: AI for Science & Safety Nodes RFP
DESCRIPTION:Umbrella request for proposals for ambitious AI-first projects 
 that make the transition to capable AI go well and use it to unlock scienc
 e. Three connected layers\, each with its own detailed call: I. Local Comp
 ute (compute that individuals or communities physically own and control)\;
  II.\n\nOrganisation: Foresight Institute\nLocation: Remote (global\; hubs
  in San Francisco and Berlin)\nAward: Typically $30\,000 to $100\,000 per 
 grant\, with smaller amounts for the Human Empowerment and AI Insurance & 
 Open Governance focus areas and higher amounts for the rest (larger possib
 le for the right project)\, plus private local compute and workspace at th
 e San Francisco or Berlin AI Nodes. No application fee.\nDuration: Project
 -based\n\nMore: https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco and Berlin)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
